---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
// Every sentence here is drawn from headquarters/marketing/licensing.md ("Copy to publish");
// the license sentence and the telemetry sentence are byte-identical to it. Change that
// document first, then this page. See "Content provenance" in CLAUDE.md.
const title = 'Turf — Licensing: free noncommercial use, pilots, production';
const description =
  'Free for noncommercial use under PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0. Companies evaluate Turf in a free 60-day pilot and license production use. One binary, no key.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="subhero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Licensing</p>
      <h1>Free for noncommercial use. Licensed for commercial use.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Turf™ is free for individuals, students, researchers, educational institutions,
        public research organizations, charities and government institutions, under the PolyForm
        Noncommercial License 1.0.0. Commercial use, including a company’s internal use, requires a
        license from Turf LLC.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="pilot">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Evaluating Turf at a company?</h2>
      <p>We offer a free 60-day evaluation under the Common Paper Pilot Agreement, a standard
        contract you can read in full at
        <a href="https://commonpaper.com/standards/pilot-agreement/1.1/">commonpaper.com/standards/pilot-agreement</a>.
        Email <a href="mailto:licensing@turf.build?subject=Pilot">licensing@turf.build</a> and we
        will send a one-page cover page.</p>
      <p>The pilot is for internal evaluation only. The binary you already have is the one you
        evaluate; there is no separate build or key. If Turf works for you, the pilot rolls into a
        production subscription.</p>
      <p class="ctas"><a class="btn primary" href="mailto:licensing@turf.build?subject=Pilot">Start a pilot</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt" id="production">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Running Turf in production?</h2>
      <p>Production use is licensed under the Common Paper Software License Agreement
        (<a href="https://commonpaper.com/standards/software-license-agreement/1.1/">commonpaper.com/standards/software-license-agreement</a>)
        with an annual subscription that includes updates, support, a conformance warranty and IP
        indemnity. Embedding Turf in your own product is available under a redistribution license;
        ask us.</p>
      <p class="ctas"><a class="btn ghost" href="mailto:licensing@turf.build?subject=Production%20license">Talk to us</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="binary">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>One binary, no license key</h2>
      <p>Every Turf build is the same binary with the same features and ships with an SBOM. There
        is no license key and nothing to unlock: a commercial license is a contract and a support
        relationship. We trust companies to license what they run.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt" id="telemetry">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Telemetry</h2>
      <p>Turf sends anonymous usage telemetry to Turf LLC by default: the version, the platform,
        counts of resources, changes and runs, and an anonymous installation id. It never sends
        resource contents, credentials, state, variable values or names. Turn it off with
        <code>turf telemetry off</code>, or with <code>TURF_TELEMETRY=off</code> or
        <code>DO_NOT_TRACK=1</code> in the engine's environment; the full field list and the endpoint
        are at <a href="/telemetry/">turf.build/telemetry</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="source">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Source</h2>
      <p>The <code>turf</code> CLI’s source, at
        <a href="https://github.com/turfbuild/turf">github.com/turfbuild/turf</a>, is licensed under
        the Mozilla Public License 2.0. Turf as a whole, the CLI together with the engine and the MCP
        server in every release archive and in the Homebrew formula, is licensed under the
        <a href="https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0">PolyForm Noncommercial
        License 1.0.0</a> (SPDX <code>PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0</code>). The license text ships in
        every release, with its required notice: Copyright Turf LLC.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt" id="questions">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Anything this page doesn’t answer: <a href="mailto:licensing@turf.build">licensing@turf.build</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* A single CTA under a prose block, spaced like the demo pages' CTA rows. */
  .ctas { margin-top: 18px; }
</style>
